l) and each bucket is capped as follows: 30% advanced reactor securities; 30% utilities securities; 35% construction and services securities; and 20% fuel securities. The components within each of these buckets are weighted according to the free-float market capitalization. A single security cap of 10% is applied for Pure Play securities and Pre-Revenue securities. Constituent weighting needs to accommodate the ability to trade a theoretical $2 billion portfolio while not exceeding an individual cap of four times their 3-month average daily trading value. Diversified securities are subject to a single security cap of 3%. Any single security that does not reach a 0.2% allocation is excluded. If a bucket or security cap is reached, excess weight is distributed proportionately among uncapped securities. No more than five securities in the Index have a weight over 4.75% and the aggregate weight of all components with a weight greater than 5% is capped at 49.5%. Effective immediately, the last paragraph of the Principal Investment Strategies section is deleted in its entirety and restated as follows: The Index is calculated and published by the Index Provider. The Index Provider is responsible for implementing the semi-annual rebalance and reconstitution and monitoring and implementing any adjustments, additions and deletions to the Index based on the index methodology and certain corporate actions, such as initial public offerings, mergers, acquisitions, bankruptcies, suspensions, de-listings, tender offers and spin-offs. The Index Provider is not affiliated with the Fund or the Adviser.","risks":[],"risk_narrative":null},"ncen":{"series":"S000083243","name":"Range Nuclear Renaissance Index ETF","lei":"529900G0IGWBAS9GIV48","acc":"0002048251-26-000876","filed":"2026-02-11","period":"2025-11-30","cik":1452937,"index":true,"index_affiliated":false,"index_exclusive":false,"multi_inverse":false,"fund_of_funds":false,"non_diversified":true,"track_diff_gross":0.14,"track_diff